(EXP-89: the documented way to turn a plain number of milliseconds into
 seconds is to divide by 1000, since EXP-88 rules `in` out.
 The second line records that the division truncates rather than rounding,
 which is the same rule as EXP-60 and matters to anyone writing the assertion.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-89.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   5
   5
)
a number called millis is 5000.
Print the millis divide 1000.
a number called awkward is 5999.
Print the awkward divide 1000.
